# Without this file, `docker compose build` (context: .) copies your LOCAL bin/ and obj/
# folders into the Linux build container via `COPY src/ src/`. If you've ever run
# `dotnet build`/`dotnet restore` on Windows in this repo, those folders contain
# Windows-specific paths (e.g. project.assets.json pointing at
# "C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages"). Copying them on top
# of the container's own (correct, Linux) restore output is exactly what caused:
#   NuGet.Packaging.Core.PackagingException: Unable to find fallback package folder
#   'C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Shared\NuGetPackages'
# Excluding bin/obj from the build context fixes it - the container always restores its own
# Linux-native copies instead of inheriting your host's.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/

# Frontend - not needed in any .NET service's build context, and node_modules is huge
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.angular/
frontend/dist/

# VCS / editor cruft
.git/
.gitignore
**/*.user

# Don't ship local env overrides into images
.env
